Camille

You continue to push the boundaries of analyses. I have never passed a data set with groups through dht2​, so I didn't know the answer to your question.

Performing an experiment with a data set that contains groups, and passing a fitted model object into dht2​, it appears dht2​ will only produce estimates of  individual density and abundance.  I've submitted an issue for our programming team to address.
https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178
 <https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178>
`dht2` cannot produce estimates of group density/abundance · Issue #178 · DistanceDevelopment/Distance <https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178>
When given data for animals observed in groups, dht2 only produces estimates of individual density and abundance. It does not produce estimates of group density or abundance. data("ClusterExercise"...
github.com <http://github.com>

The work-around you propose (remove (or rename)) the size column will work as long as group size is not involved in the detection function modelling.
